  "limitations": [
    "Database transactions cannot make an external provider effect atomic, recall an already-sent request, or supply a general compensation workflow. Post-call cancellation remains best effort.",
    "Cancellation transition effect counts are an exact cancellation-time snapshot. Final effect truth comes from immutable action history because a bounded call may succeed or become outcome-unknown after the Run is cancelled.",
    "Provider idempotency prevents authorized replay where supported but does not establish external exactly-once effects. A late provider receipt is not used to rewrite an already immutable outcome-unknown action.",
    "AuditContext provides integrity-checked pseudonymous provenance but does not authenticate a cancellation caller. No public cancellation route, role enforcement, CSRF control, or HTTP error mapping is claimed here.",
    "The ordered persistence timeline covers Run, Step, and ExternalAction facts. The complete operator timeline and UI projection remain RUN-06 and AC-14 scope.",
    "Tests use deterministic adapters, injected clocks, and file-backed SQLite rather than a production worker fleet, live external provider, or distributed contention environment.",
    "The audit constraint now represents cancellation after any provider-retry generation. No Alembic migration is added; PostgreSQL runtime locking and migration rollout remain unexecuted."
  ]
